# Git commits – no co-author

When running `git commit` (or suggesting commit messages):

- **Do not** add a `Co-authored-by:` trailer.
- **Do not** use `--author` or any option that attributes the commit to anyone other than the repository owner.
- Use only: `git commit -m "message"` (or equivalent) with the user’s chosen message.

The user has not authorized Cursor/agent to be listed as co-author on commits.
